    "name": "shMON/USDC market: shMON cap, USDC rate curve, and the WMON vault for the shMON vaults' market maker (Monad)",
    "description": "1) eshMON-4 0x2f22C096651BBc97e63B459a561f2416b2F33e81 supply cap to 200,000,000 shMON (raw 12826); borrow cap stays raw 1, no borrowing. 2) eUSDC-24 0xdE5870224123d974258Ce4501c8b045375d2054a to the IRMLinearKinky curve 0xe743F06a8A2Dcc9565926a9b11513e957e1897c6: at 80% use borrowers pay 8.5%, at 90% they pay 9.6% and lenders earn 7.7% after the 10% fee. 3) The router 0x52d30dbf4e3209F2666982A47e216e0aA3D9518e prices WMON with the same RedStone MON feed already inside shMON's price, 0x03e574FAD8b74FE9DA7F32d709bD881A6e8eF2dE. 4) The router prices the new WMON vault eWMON-14 0xfE26b4EE9e7000e06B7Cb2fc614A4526e845e702 by its shares (deployed and set by the AlphaGrowth deployer, governor already this Safe: 116M WMON supply cap, 104M borrow cap, 20% rate at no use and 30% at the 90% kink, lends 97/98 against eshMON-4 and against each unstaking shMON vault, 79/80 against eUSDC-24, 10% fee, 15% liquidation discount). 5) eUSDC-24 lends 79/80 against eWMON-14, as it does against eshMON-4. 6) and 7) The router prices the two unstaking shMON vaults by their shares (shMON held plus MON on its way back from shMonad's unstake): 0x59f7f897322D5FdEFCa38beB78137559eD985F80 for the shmon-neverland-usdc-hl vault's exit desk and 0xc0CA1086131046766956bBD030fe9595Cc8204a1 for shmon-neverland-usdt0-hl's. Rehearsed as the Safe on a Monad fork with a 500,000 gas limit per transaction; automatic estimates come up short.",
